    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "Base-model results are omitted but declared in rows_left_out. LLaMA-3.1-Base 8B→70B shows 0-shot r .178→.187 with MAE worsening 25.44→31.79, a weak size effect that a researcher may want added. The evidence is a few model points on one downstream regression task, with deterministic decoding and no curve fit. The verdicts are qualitative statements about monotonic improvement, not about predictability in the scaling-law sense."
  },
